<!-- 2026-09-25 (simulator/desktop/jetbrains finding): despite the scheme name
     and originalScheme below, every accent hex here (CARET_COLOR/DEFAULT_KEYWORD
     C0E3C0, SELECTION_BACKGROUND A6C9A6, DEFAULT_CLASS_NAME/DEFAULT_NUMBER 89A889)
     is the SAGE variant's accent_hi/accent/accent_alt, not lime's (C1FF58/A8E635/
     8BC406): tokens/out/json-tokens.json's default_variant is sage, and three
     of four accent families already matched it exactly. LINE_NUMBERS_COLOR/
     DEFAULT_LINE_COMMENT/etc were 6B7280 and DEFAULT_DOC_COMMENT was 9CA3AF:
     neither is any current token; both are now sage's text_muted (7F8695),
     collapsing the doc/regular-comment shade difference (FONT_TYPE italic still
     distinguishes doc comments). DEFAULT_STRING/GUTTER_VCS_NEW/DIFF_INSERTED
     were 71F79F (lime's positive), not sage's (3FFABB). ERRORS_ATTRIBUTES/
     BAD_CHARACTER/DIFF_CONFLICT/etc were ED254E, not sage's negative (F42E53).
     Fixed all four to the tokens they already read as everywhere else in this
     file. Left the "Lime Glass" name/metadata alone: renaming a scheme's own
     identity is a bigger call than a hex fix; see the simulator run's report.
     SELECTION_FOREGROUND was FFFFFF over SELECTION_BACKGROUND's A6C9A6 (sage
     accent, a light pastel green): 1.72:1, nowhere near the 4.5:1 floor real
     highlighted text needs. accent is a light fill, so it needs a dark
     foreground, not a lighter one: base (07080A) measures 11.0:1 on it, so
     SELECTION_FOREGROUND is now base's hex, the same fix pattern GRUB's
     card_fill and the KDE layer's editSelectionText() both use for a light
     accent fill. -->
